# Week 2 - NumPy and Pandas

## Overview

During Week 2, I practiced NumPy and pandas for working with arrays, numerical calculations, datasets, data cleaning, and basic data analysis.

## NumPy Concepts Learned

- Creating 1D and 2D arrays
- Checking shape, size, and dimensions
- Array indexing and slicing
- Addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division
- Reshaping and flattening arrays
- Generating random integers and floats
- Mean, median, and standard deviation
- Matrix addition and multiplication

## Pandas Concepts Learned

- Creating pandas Series
- Indexing and filtering Series
- Creating DataFrames from dictionaries and lists
- Reading and writing CSV files
- Using head(), tail(), info(), and describe()
- Selecting single and multiple columns
- Filtering rows using conditions
- Identifying missing values
- Filling and dropping missing values
- Renaming columns
- Sorting records
- Creating calculated columns
- Using groupby() for counts and averages
- Cleaning and analyzing a small dataset

